  "comments": "MTO coins exist:<br />\r\n- 2542 MTO sets of copper-silver-gold, 16~18 sets believed to be made. (set of copper-silver-gold 1 Satang to 5 Baht series)<br />\r\n- Coins dated 2540 struck on Aluminium planchet exist; PCGS <a href=\"https://www.pcgs.com/cert/80717148\" rel=\"nofollow\">#80717148</a>, PCGS <a href=\"https://www.pcgs.com/cert/80717148\" rel=\"nofollow\">#80763607</a>, PCGS <a href=\"https://www.pcgs.com/cert/37982047\" rel=\"nofollow\">#37982047</a>. (set of aluminium 25-50 Satang 2540)<br />\r\n- Coins struck as double obverse; PCGS <a href=\"https://www.pcgs.com/cert/80717153\" rel=\"nofollow\">#80717153</a>, NGC <a href=\"https://www.ngccoin.com/certlookup/4623208-001/64/\" rel=\"nofollow\">#4623208-001</a>. (set of double obverse and double reverse 25-50 Satang 2532)<br />\r\n- Coins dated 2532 struck as double reverse; PCGS <a href=\"https://www.pcgs.com/cert/80717154\" rel=\"nofollow\">#80717154</a>. (set of double obverse and double reverse 25-50 Satang 2532)<br />\r\n- Coin dated 2532 struck as medal alignment; PCGS <a href=\"https://www.pcgs.com/cert/80717159\" rel=\"nofollow\">#80717159</a>. (set of medal alignment 25 Satang to 5 Baht 2532)",
